Z||000004||CoolBlue87GT||07-23-2001||09:21 AM||||    <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by AusFiero:<BR><B>now you tell me I have to have red nuts to do it.      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>LOL LOL LOL LOL LOL LOL LOL LOL <P>Don't know about the red ones, I do have one question on the subject on "Valve cap covers"<P>While I was at the Carlisle show, someone told me the "Grey valve caps covers" on my Blue 87 GT were very rare, and that I should take them off overnight, as someone would steal them.<P>Are they that rare ?  I never heard this before.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Dsc00101.jpg"> <BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/CoolBlue87GT.gif">   <BR><p>[This message has been edited by CoolBlue87GT (edited 07-23-2001).]||||reg||6
Z||000005||Philphine||07-23-2001||10:48 AM||||just took a quick look at mine. regular black caps. didn't notice anything that seemed like residue from a sticker being on there before.||||reg||1
Z||000006||PBJ||07-23-2001||10:56 AM||||CoolBlue87GT:<P>grey caps mean that they are the orignal caps. GM factory caps for many years up till about 5 years ago had grey caps.  They are only different because of color-I would not remove them at night.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Toddster||07-23-2001||11:47 AM||||I think it was a mistake. Pontiac may have experimented with the idea but when it came time to produce the cars theycame with plain lug caps like all the other fieros. I bought an Indy with 13k miles that had been garaged for 15 years in original condition and it had the black lug caps.||||reg||1
